{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "Q61337", "uniProtkbId": "BAD_MOUSE", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1997-11-01", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-11-04", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "1996-11-01", "entryVersion": 197, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Mus musculus", "commonName": "Mouse", "taxonId": 10090, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Glires", "Rodentia", "Myomorpha", "Muroidea", "Muridae", "Murinae", "Mus", "Mus"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"value": "Bcl2-associated agonist of cell death"}, "shortNames": [{"value": "BAD"}]}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"value": "Bcl-2-binding component 6"}}, {"fullName": {"value": "Bcl-xL/Bcl-2-associated death promoter"}}, {"fullName": {"value": "Bcl2 antagonist of cell death"}}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"value": "Bad"}, "synonyms": [{"value": "Bbc6"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"value": "Promotes cell death. Successfully competes for the binding to Bcl-X(L), Bcl-2 and Bcl-W, thereby affecting the level of heterodimerization of these proteins with BAX. Can reverse the death repressor activity of Bcl-X(L), but not that of Bcl-2. Appears to act as a link between growth factor receptor signaling and the apoptotic pathways"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "O35147"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "16509771"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "21546903"}], "value": "Forms heterodimers with the anti-apoptotic proteins, Bcl-X(L), Bcl-2 and Bcl-W. Also binds protein S100A10 (By similarity). The Ser-112/Ser-136 phosphorylated form binds 14-3-3 proteins. Interacts with AKT1 and PIM3 (By similarity). Interacts (via BH3 domain) with NOL3 (via CARD domain); preventing the association of BAD with BCL2 (By similarity). Interacts with HIF3A isoform 2 (via C-terminus domain); the interaction reduces the binding between BAD and BAX (PubMed:21546903). Interacts with GIMAP3/IAN4 and GIMAP5/IAN5 (PubMed:16509771)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "INTERACTION", "interactions": [{"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q61337", "intActId": "EBI-400328"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q64373-1", "geneName": "Bcl2l1", "intActId": "EBI-526380"}, "numberOfExperiments": 2, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q61337", "intActId": "EBI-400328"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P10415", "geneName": "BCL2", "intActId": "EBI-77694"}, "numberOfExperiments": 6, "organismDiffer": true}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q61337", "intActId": "EBI-400328"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q07817-1", "geneName": "BCL2L1", "intActId": "EBI-287195"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": true}, {"interactantOne": {"uniProtKBAccession": "Q61337", "intActId": "EBI-400328"}, "interactantTwo": {"uniProtKBAccession": "P63104", "geneName": "YWHAZ", "intActId": "EBI-347088"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": true}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "note": {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "21546903"}], "value": "Colocalizes with HIF3A isoform 2 in the cytoplasm (PubMed:21546903). Upon phosphorylation, locates to the cytoplasm"}]}, "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"value": "Mitochondrion outer membrane", "id": "SL-0172"}}, {"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "21546903"}], "value": "Cytoplasm", "id": "SL-0086"}}]}, {"texts": [{"value": "Intact BH3 motif is required by BIK, BID, BAK, BAD and BAX for their pro-apoptotic activity and for their interaction with anti-apoptotic members of the Bcl-2 family"}], "commentType": "DOMAIN"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10611223"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10679322"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11278362"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11342610"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11493700"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11717309"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "12954615"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "15849194"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9381178"}], "value": "Phosphorylated on one or more of Ser-112, Ser-136, Ser-155 and Ser-170 in response to survival stimuli, which blocks its pro-apoptotic activity. Phosphorylation on Ser-136 or Ser-112 promotes heterodimerization with 14-3-3 proteins. This interaction then facilitates the phosphorylation at Ser-155, a site within the BH3 motif, leading to the release of Bcl-X(L) and the promotion of cell survival. Ser-136 is the major site of AKT/PKB phosphorylation, Ser-155 the major site of protein kinase A (CAPK) phosphorylation"}], "commentType": "PTM"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10611223"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10679322"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11342610"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "11493700"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9381178"}], "value": "Methylation at Arg-131 and Arg-133 by PRMT1 inhibits Akt-mediated phosphorylation at Ser-136"}], "commentType": "PTM"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the Bcl-2 family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "The protein name 'Bcl2 antagonist of cell death' may be misleading. The protein antagonises Bcl2-mediated repression of cell death, hence it promotes apoptosis"}], "commentType": "CAUTION"}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 204, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Bcl2-associated agonist of cell death", "featureId": "PRO_0000143104"}, {"type": "Region", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 138, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Disordered", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "SAM", "id": "MobiDB-lite"}]}, {"type": "Region", "location": {"start": {"value": 160, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 179, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Disordered", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "SAM", "id": "MobiDB-lite"}]}, {"type": "Motif", "location": {"start": {"value": 147, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 161, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "BH3"}, {"type": "Compositional bias", "location": {"start": {"value": 85, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 97, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Polar residues", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "SAM", "id": "MobiDB-lite"}]}, {"type": "Compositional bias", "location": {"start": {"value": 117, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 127, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Acidic residues", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "SAM", "id": "MobiDB-lite"}]}, {"type": "Modified residue", "location": {"start": {"value": 67, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 67, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Phosphoserine", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "Q92934"}]}, {"type": "Modified residue", "location": {"start": {"value": 112, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 112, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Phosphoserine; by PKA, PKB, PIM2, PIM3, PAK1, PAK2, PAK4, PAK5, RPS6KA1 and RAF1", "evidences": [{"evid